## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to extend a simple Azure Fundamentals stack with real feature-flag patterns, connecting front-end and back-end behavior to centralized configuration while maintaining security best practices.

## Key Concepts

- Azure App Configuration service and feature flags
- Front-end integration with App Configuration JavaScript SDK
- Server-side access via Azure AD managed identity
- GitHub Actions for infrastructure and configuration deployment
- Latency, caching, and cost optimization considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Front-end: fetch feature flag from App Configuration
const featureFlags = await fetchFeatureFlags();
if (featureFlags.enableWidget) {
  renderWidget();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire basic observability across static web apps, serverless functions, and a database, a foundational skill for troubleshooting in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Application Insights integration on SPA and Function
- Correlation IDs across SPA -> Function -> SQL
- Log Analytics queries to join telemetry and database logs
- End-to-end request tracing and basic dashboards

## Code Example
```javascript
// SPA instrumentation and correlationId
import { ApplicationInsights } from "@microsoft/applicationinsights-web";
const appInsights = new ApplicationInsights({ config: { instrumentationKey: "<ikey>" } });
appInsights.loadAppInsights();
const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();
fetch("/api/feedback", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "X-Correlation-Id": correlationId, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ text, rating })
});
```

```csharp
// Function: read header and insert into SQL with correlationId
string corr = req.Headers["X-Correlation-Id"];
using (var cmd = new SqlCommand("INSERT INTO Feedback (Text, CorrId) VALUES (@t, @c)", conn)) {
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@t", text);
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@c", corr);
  cmd.ExecuteNonQuery();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the correlation path in Log Analytics?
- How would you handle missing correlation IDs in edge cases?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design end-to-end scalable ingestion with strong isolation and cost discipline, plus onboarding automation.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation strategies (namespaces, resource groups)
- Ingestion options (IoT Hub vs Event Hubs) and scaling
- Data encryption with CMK and Key Vault
- RBAC, Service Principals, least privilege
- Onboarding automation (ARM/Bicep/Terraform), CI/CD
- Monitoring, auditing, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo onboarding snippet (illustrative only)
async function onboardTenant(tenantId){
  await createEventHubNamespace(`tenant-${tenantId}-eh`);
  await createStorageAccount(`tenant${tenantId}sa`);
  await assignRBAC(tenantId, 'Contributor');
  await configureCMK(`tenant-${tenantId}-cmk`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation boundaries at scale?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant storage vs a shared data lake with tagging?
